From bf4e3259024f2116fa83cab1089a3ffa72e35a44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:31:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 11/18] fix(js): honour MutationObserver attributeFilter and
 observe() options

MutationObserver ignored attributeFilter, so an observer that watches only
`src` and rewrites `type`/`class` from its callback was told about its own
writes and re-ran forever. OneTrust's OtAutoBlock on booking.com does exactly
that to a dynamically inserted gtm.js: an endless microtask chain that pinned a
core and grew the engine by 13-70 MB/s (2.5 GB after 190 s, no end).

observe() now follows DOM "observe": attributeFilter and old-value options
imply their type, invalid options throw TypeError, re-observing a node replaces
its options instead of registering twice, and attributeOldValue reports the
old value. Records are queued per interested observer and delivered from one
mutation observer microtask.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
